/**
  @page examples-geometry-index Mesh geometry examples
  @brief Create a mesh, then inspect its topological relations.

  These examples establish the geometric data needed before fields and
  equations can be defined. They use generated meshes, so no external mesh
  files are needed to begin.

  1. @subpage examples-geometry-uniformgrid — Create structured meshes and
     control their physical dimensions.
  2. @subpage examples-geometry-connectivity — Compute and inspect incidence
     relations between vertices, edges, and cells.

  3. @subpage examples-interface-traces — Evaluate a discontinuous field from
     each side of an interior facet.

  4. @subpage examples-eikonal-fmm — Compute arrival times and check them
     against an analytic point-source solution.

  5. @subpage examples-distance-normalization — Normalize a signed Poisson
     field and compare it with an analytic geometric reference.

  The @ref guides-meshes "mesh guide" covers traversal and queries; the
  @ref guides-polytopes "polytope guide" explains reference elements and mappings.

  @m_footernavigation
*/
